<title>TAIWAN: TAIWAN SUGAR BUYS 30,000T OF US CORN/SOY AT TENDER.</title>
<headline>TAIWAN SUGAR BUYS 30,000T OF US CORN/SOY AT TENDER.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Taiwan Sugar Corp bought a combined shipment of 20,000 tonnes U.S. corn and 10,000 of U.S. soybeans from Continental at a tender on Wednesday, traders said.  </p>
<p>Details for the tender are as follows:</p>
<p>		     U.S. Gulf  Pacific N.W. Prices/Futures</p>
<p> Corn    20,000  Sep 16-30  Oct 1-15     95.75 US cents/Dec</p>
<p> Soybean 10,000  Sep 16-30  Oct 1-15     US$298.78/CNF</p>
<p>-- Taipei newsroom (886) 2-508-0815; Fax (886) 2-508-0204</p>
